message.content:
{
  "agent_id": "spec_coordinator",
  "narrative": "Reviewed the current starter implementation in src/task_query.py and the SPEC.md placeholder. The existing function only supports simple offset/limit, status filtering, and case‑sensitive title substring search, which fails many acceptance tests (search normalization, NFKC casefold, whitespace handling, priority sorting, pagination after filtering, negative limit/offset handling, unknown status rejection, etc.). The SPEC.md currently contains only a high‑level description without concrete step mapping. I have identified the remaining open issues: requirements clarification, search normalization, filtering order, and acceptance review. No code changes have been made yet; the next development step will implement full query handling according to the acceptance criteria, update SPEC.md with detailed function steps, and then run the test suite.",
  "completion_declared": false,
  "state": {
    "open_issue_ids": [
      "requirements",
      "search-normalization",
      "filtering-order",
      "acceptance-review"
    ],
    "info_items": [
      "Current implementation lacks NFKC casefold search, whitespace normalization, priority sorting, and proper pagination after filtering.",
      "Negative limit and offset values are not validated, leading to test failures.",
      "Status handling does not reject unknown statuses as required.",
      "SPEC.md needs detailed mapping of acceptance criteria to function steps and user‑facing messages."
    ],
    "reasons": {}
  }
}

